---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { criteria, questions } from "../../data/program";

// Current Work page (A3g §6). Route stays /research; the displayed H1 and title
// are "Current Work". Begins with the current problem, not the global identity.
const selectedWork = [
  {
    title: "Three Ways of Leaving <em>p</em> Unsettled",
    meta: "Semantics paper · construct under review",
    href: null,
    current: true,
    desc: "Compares <em>might p</em>, <em>might p or might not p</em>, and <em>I don’t know whether p</em>, asking how each changes the discourse and which replies it licenses. No results yet; the construct brief is under review by a formal semanticist.",
  },
  {
    title: "Master’s thesis: learning these distinctions",
    meta: "Thesis · in design",
    href: null,
    desc: "Asks whether a small language model can acquire the same distinctions from developmentally realistic text, and which patterns in the input are needed for them to emerge. Begins with the formal analysis above.",
  },
  {
    title: "Cross-lingual ProtoBias",
    meta: "First-author paper · in revision for arXiv",
    href: "/research/cross-lingual-protobias",
    desc: "Holds each image pair fixed and varies the prompt language to test when vision-language judges follow semantic fit and when they fall back on culturally specific prototypes. About 12,600 judgments across seven languages and two model families; code is public.",
  },
  {
    title: "Latent Control States",
    meta: "Collaboration · DFKI",
    href: null,
    desc: "With DFKI, asks whether prompt framing changes only a model’s answer or also a causally relevant internal state. My role: I designed the utilitarian minimal-pair experiment varying dilemma, benefit size, and framing.",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Current Work · Xiaochuan Li"
  description="How epistemic possibility expressions such as might affect later reasoning: does might only lower a speaker's commitment, or does it keep a particular possibility available? The current construct, its diagnostics, honest status, and selected work."
>
  <article class="cw">
    <h1 class="cw-h1">Current Work</h1>
    <p class="cw-lede">
      I am developing a semantic account of how epistemic possibility expressions affect later
      reasoning. The central contrast is simple: does <em>might</em> only lower a speaker’s
      commitment, or does it keep a particular possibility in play?
    </p>

    <section class="cw-sec">
      <h2 class="cw-h2">The linguistic problem</h2>
      <p class="cw-p">Consider three answers to the question “Where is the key?”</p>
      <ol class="cw-ex">
        <li>It <em>might</em> be in the drawer.</li>
        <li>It <em>might</em> be in the drawer, or it might not.</li>
        <li>I <em>don’t know whether</em> it is in the drawer.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="cw-p">
        All three leave the key’s location unresolved, but they need not do the same discourse work. A
        modal assertion introduces a possibility. A disjunction makes both sides explicit. An
        ignorance report describes what the speaker cannot settle. My current paper asks how these
        utterances differ in the commitments they create and the replies they license.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="cw-sec">
      <h2 class="cw-h2">What would count as evidence</h2>
      <p class="cw-p">
        Before testing the proposal, I need an observable difference between a maintained possibility
        and ordinary uncertainty. I use three criteria:
      </p>
      <ul class="cw-crit">
        {criteria.map((c) => (
          <li>{c.name}: {c.text}.</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="cw-p">
        Evidence-sensitivity is crucial. If a possibility remains active even after it has been ruled
        out, the effect may be simple perseveration rather than semantic maintenance. The design
        therefore holds the available information fixed, varies the linguistic framing, and measures
        comprehension instead of assuming it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="cw-sec">
      <h2 class="cw-h2">Two empirical questions</h2>
      <div class="cw-qs">
        {questions.map((q) => (
          <div class="cw-q">
            <p class="cw-q-label">{q.label}</p>
            <p class="cw-q-text">{q.text}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="cw-p">
        These questions require different evidence. The developmental question concerns human
        acquisition. The computational question asks what linguistic distribution can support in a
        controlled learner. A language model is useful for the second question; it is not a proxy for
        a developing child.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="cw-sec">
      <h2 class="cw-h2">Current status</h2>
      <p class="cw-status">
        The project is still at the construct stage. A formal semanticist is reviewing the brief that
        defines the theoretical contrast and the diagnostics. The developmental literature review is
        under way, and no behavioural or model study has yet produced a result.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="cw-sec">
      <h2 class="cw-h2">Selected work</h2>
      <div class="cw-projs">
        {selectedWork.map((p) => (
          <div class={`cw-proj${p.current ? " cw-proj-current" : ""}`}>
            <div class="cw-proj-top">
              {p.href
                ? <a class="cw-proj-title" href={p.href} set:html={p.title} />
                : <span class="cw-proj-title-plain" set:html={p.title} />}
              <span class="cw-proj-meta">{p.meta}</span>
            </div>
            <p class="cw-proj-desc" set:html={p.desc} />
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .cw { max-width: 42rem; }
  .cw-h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 0 0 0.9rem; color: var(--color-text); }
  .cw-lede { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-text); margin: 0 0 1rem; max-width: 40rem; }
  .cw-lede em { font-style: italic; }

  .cw-sec { margin-top: 2.8rem; }
  .cw-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-dim);
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.6rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .cw-p { font-size: 0.96rem; line-height: 1.72; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .cw-p em { font-style: italic; color: var(--color-text); }

  .cw-ex {
    list-style: decimal;
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem 1rem 2.6rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
  }
  .cw-ex li { margin: 0.25rem 0; color: var(--color-text); line-height: 1.6; }
  .cw-ex em { font-style: italic; }

  .cw-crit { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; padding: 0; }
  .cw-crit li {
    padding: 0.55rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  .cw-crit li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .cw-crit strong { color: var(--color-text); font-weight: 600; }

  .cw-qs { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .cw-qs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .cw-q { border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; }
  .cw-q-label { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.13em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-text-dim); margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .cw-q-text { font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--color-text); margin: 0; }

  .cw-status {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
  }

  .cw-projs { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .cw-proj { padding: 1.05rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .cw-proj:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .cw-proj-top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .cw-proj-title { font-size: 1.02rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: none; }
  .cw-proj-title:hover { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .cw-proj-title-plain { font-size: 1.02rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--color-text); }
  .cw-proj-title em, .cw-proj-title-plain em { font-style: italic; }
  .cw-proj-meta { flex: none; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-text-dim); white-space: nowrap; }
  .cw-proj-current .cw-proj-meta { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .cw-proj-desc { font-size: 0.93rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin: 0; max-width: 60ch; }
  .cw-proj-desc em { font-style: italic; }
</style>
